From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sun, 5 Mar 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: Duel.MPTurnOwns(c) tells the owner of a controlled card
 from the other opponents at n > 2

The Lua values 0 and 1 fold every opponent to 1, so a script cannot tell the owner of a stolen card from another opponent.
Snatch Steal asked its controller for an opponent pick in every opponent Standby Phase and gave the LP to the picked seat.

Duel.MPTurnOwns(c) is true when the turn player is the real owner of c and is alive. It asks nothing, so a condition may call
it. When it is true and the owner is an opponent of the scope duelist, it binds that owner (first binding wins), so that the
Recover(1, ...) of the same scope gains the LP of exactly that seat (Tag: the team LP of the owner). Additive: no existing
function changes, and the function is used only by the overlay (loaded at 3 or 4 seats).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
---
 libduel.cpp | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libduel.cpp b/libduel.cpp
index 5449f0c..197d1ab 100644
--- a/libduel.cpp
+++ b/libduel.cpp
@@ -4987,6 +4987,25 @@ LUA_STATIC_FUNCTION(MPBindSeat) {
 	lua_pushboolean(L, usable);
 	return 1;
 }
+// Duel.MPTurnOwns(c): true when the turn player is the real OWNER of the card c and is alive. The Lua values 0 and 1 fold every
+// opponent to 1, so a script cannot tell the owner of a stolen card from another opponent: this is the seat compare. It asks
+// nothing, so a condition may call it. When it gives true and the owner is an opponent of the scope duelist, it also binds that
+// owner (first binding wins, as for every bind), so that a later Lua 1 of the same scope is exactly that owner (Snatch Steal: only
+// the owner of the stolen monster gains the LP, in the Standby Phase of that owner; Tag: the exact seat, not the partner).
+// Two seats: the plain compare (no scope folds).
+LUA_STATIC_FUNCTION(MPTurnOwns) {
+	check_param_count(L, 1);
+	const auto* pcard = lua_get<card*, true>(L, 1);
+	const auto& f = *pduel->game_field;
+	const uint8_t owner = pcard->owner;
+	const bool yes = owner == f.infos.turn_player && (f.n_duelists <= 2 || f.is_alive(owner));
+	if(yes) {
+		if(const auto* s = f7_scope(pduel); s && !f.same_team(s->P, owner))
+			pduel->lua->scope_bind(owner);
+	}
+	lua_pushboolean(L, yes);
+	return 1;
+}
 }
 }
 
